#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161772 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "59ea7ebb-5b69-5551-a5b9-c286e2730881" :question/math-academy-id "e-8160" :question/problem "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](images/af/af5a3add30b403955409fc5c9315f2607a432461e85e4b129e37e0f8e55245a9.svg)  Evaluate the function when ![](images/ae/aee097401481134f5802be4cba03f62ff46cf5fd0f4860fc85e7a85596d3ae09.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Substituting ![](images/8d/8d6326ecf66d2e20be5893c256b05f45cf986f00aa332e5b2e343a79096af202.svg) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161773 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "30204c69-3362-5cc1-a04a-3bb83559b300" :question/math-academy-id "e-8161" :question/problem "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when ![](images/e3/e355ba8664f980f8e06bcbda40adf063d376478e745b9b6b036331a895192c54.svg) and ![](images/7f/7fe125bd6366adb85e10ab5719049e1e0db7c719b4a714f9155efee77a8f604b.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](images/14/14418dfa570c1be7015799f009ad93388a6dd6d04bed48972bc8163351bbeb87.svg) and ![](images/8b/8bc4748c7c554dc1edfbdce567f9e6d994ebe0955346bfa34712e20286aaa3b3.svg) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161774 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "34398117-07f4-51d9-a879-30a0f6891e68" :question/math-academy-id "e-8162" :question/problem "![](images/75/7505a6fdbe31e7e3e35e1b9b393d04753b0ccd534e5bacda199e8fc902a5fe3c.svg)\nConsider the matrix ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](images/50/50fa4bc1260a734d8f2a1c3045c81dd58e5148d81b6bd85e901c492ab4f61ead.svg) in terms of the components of ![](images/2c/2c28ae197ea4a26ad524d5e6cc89a18a21bf6f215b14432d5377fb3c8a287b6f.svg) and ![](images/35/356a4d35d556458edf899d2b0a49d6db2d47743c0d029c58e1bd3a3b88d9b8c9.svg)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](images/b6/b6e5dec69a4614a003b3e1e77d18dfb6747cf556fa6f1374803ab0ffc765a3cb.svg) of ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) corresponds to the term ![](images/6e/6e2dccb072d3420de2a0d2d4c9ad9b3f3ff44f62a59c0b3580ced4cdc42f9c9e.svg) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](images/c3/c3b74ef5a2e970298bd4117c499d18a7bc3319c5e4d4c05b83e0e25fb18fba30.svg)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](images/aa/aa4630ec70bc3741e32a93d26aa15090e187b8e660ce611bc80e20e2bd8114e8.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161775 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161983 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/id #uuid "84e1b597-45d7-51f4-aaa9-8a52c753a510" :question/math-academy-id "e-8163" :question/problem "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](images/44/443b1cf1d4425f83b834101627dd202732cf2c905848c8ddbb93dd518f3b35db.svg)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b71e7f5-e589-5173-b8d1-5bca4549c39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269660} {:answer/id #uuid "47b1a8af-7aea-532c-8d7e-ec9ca4a680a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269919} {:answer/id #uuid "8edbc905-d6c8-5d53-b939-9b29819d4197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270508} {:answer/id #uuid "b07da744-4817-52a4-9472-01482b684293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270842} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a6607f-78a6-5636-bb3a-99fd1012c614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b71e7f5-e589-5173-b8d1-5bca4549c39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269660} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddf57b9b-e627-50e0-b1ee-e1548d6dfec5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7a2955a-d0ed-5f0b-a82c-5ef03bbf9550" :question/math-academy-id "q-140851" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-5+4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e179630-a47a-54c8-a994-33d07597762f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269521} {:answer/id #uuid "3592eac6-b1b2-514f-b1c0-230e4d054819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269759} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbb606b-d502-546a-9c9b-7f1f84ba1bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269988} {:answer/id #uuid "839850ab-34ae-5253-8727-21e3f2303e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270406} {:answer/id #uuid "a270baaf-98f0-5ed4-a01e-9d526d00752b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3592eac6-b1b2-514f-b1c0-230e4d054819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269759} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7b09c8-3189-5ed7-afb9-4ecd048bffce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1823b0b-dd9b-5b00-861c-14c6a4bab473" :question/math-academy-id "q-140853" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e110b97-5ab5-5617-aa1a-9f75fa92ce22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269391} {:answer/id #uuid "284ebe93-9d33-5b44-86a9-d99931234376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269630} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9dfa71-ca6b-59de-8143-11e3be4e3df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269943} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ba7f9a-5b96-5112-9756-284a5a5f9e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270872} {:answer/id #uuid "d8197c76-cd41-58f6-8a5a-d3b5c0bf37ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e110b97-5ab5-5617-aa1a-9f75fa92ce22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269391} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac61f25-e40e-52f8-bb85-65ad8a3cc3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271923}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "806f88a5-c472-5e05-ba98-6e9ea06c0751" :question/math-academy-id "q-140861" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 20\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161983 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37fbf637-f056-50e2-b26c-d48cd839d327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423314} {:answer/id #uuid "43f4a623-1435-5ed2-ab63-86eb0d268aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423315} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef974e9-9b7e-5867-a2a8-3b0562672573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423328} {:answer/id #uuid "bf99ec69-37cc-5e99-a769-8cf0e13875fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423336} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a888cc-2671-524d-89a1-f86fe165eae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ef974e9-9b7e-5867-a2a8-3b0562672573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423328} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f518492-fe4d-57a1-9b58-5b5c3a48afb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a33de8e7-0315-5081-b30e-a76239172d51" :question/math-academy-id "q-140864" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & b & -2 \\\\ c & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b-c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b-c=3+(-5)-(-2)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55277d69-eedc-5c5c-883a-083746e00947" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Bilinear Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e5bf9a-2ab7-5739-b14d-f546e211c130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423302} {:answer/id #uuid "46905384-ce8a-5ab9-af0b-2976fe3be6b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423316} {:answer/id #uuid "989ea25f-37be-568e-b80b-e6e58c5da663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423329} {:answer/id #uuid "aaeac9ef-7f69-5e21-b596-8a8eced51973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423332} {:answer/id #uuid "eb109607-0a7d-5ec5-83c6-08f21eea7ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "989ea25f-37be-568e-b80b-e6e58c5da663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423329} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c44a10-398e-5901-bd28-38e9099fece6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "734f0c5e-0d8c-5660-90a8-1dd3058abdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-93684" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({y}_{1}-2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161983 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60cd05d-e4af-5bf1-8827-cab48da934f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065d3589-3788-5175-ad2e-ca115572f162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354707} {:answer/id #uuid "67df311e-165a-597e-b288-ad0f5f0b6045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355584} {:answer/id #uuid "a193fd48-d649-5aa5-9966-9c43b7ea4461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356102} {:answer/id #uuid "a3379ff6-3b09-55dd-bf18-e79be3b7a15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356110} {:answer/id #uuid "d78cb865-9e7f-5234-9e23-e2cf29601927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67df311e-165a-597e-b288-ad0f5f0b6045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355584} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3a5fb3-8ee9-561c-b9ce-d7ccb5a0bd22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82537968-6767-565c-820b-eb7ee2eb1460" :question/math-academy-id "q-93685" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+(-1)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34791725-9520-5f7a-ab6c-9218c24779dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355129} {:answer/id #uuid "8360267f-4c94-52e2-add6-b66758050ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355822} {:answer/id #uuid "864a7748-78b9-5775-a445-8883818a7bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355854} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cd7411-29a8-51dc-a036-7178cb9e0874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356670} {:answer/id #uuid "ef79d3b4-b24e-5d4c-b7ba-68c2f302db08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "864a7748-78b9-5775-a445-8883818a7bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355854} :answer-field/id #uuid "da01e0af-4eb5-5d89-b320-97ae18e3c7cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "689d9753-4018-5be8-9d81-e1a605de8efc" :question/math-academy-id "q-93900" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$   Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =12-8 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423306} {:answer/id #uuid "276907f5-ae34-5479-a1e4-a7f16d57caea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423309} {:answer/id #uuid "6146082e-e480-5b7d-b409-a06184533a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423322} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d0a514-3a53-5e57-ba88-4694b5408ef1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423335} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2ff817-5b1d-5fce-bb2e-2c85c38b3269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c795eca-acf3-51bc-b2c7-4a595a93aa2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423306} :answer-field/id #uuid "25010ff5-ab1c-5a8c-a044-e8048ed684a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cffcafb-88aa-554a-9e0e-d0b676da85d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-93906" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ \\,2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10-8-3+4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7083d465-9871-59ca-97fa-583e740e961f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Bilinear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423305} {:answer/id #uuid "21bd4957-61ca-515f-955c-429ec430a2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423307} {:answer/id #uuid "4c939ced-410b-538a-b95e-7eabbbc8766a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423318} {:answer/id #uuid "56aa150d-8b20-5d1a-b78e-808ac608f56f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423320} {:answer/id #uuid "66b821eb-cfc5-5167-9c91-37e6e80d6d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d0649e-68ce-5666-85e2-10cd035eb702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423305} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bb5e8f5-c9f7-536e-9428-9ca34ec2e366" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc56657a-b79e-53ee-87cf-34f486cb39d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-93920" :question/problem "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}. \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-0+0-1-2 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e71b8aa-1ba1-5eb2-8b28-0544642b8d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354799} {:answer/id #uuid "3301950e-31e1-5006-a9a1-c376c16b2a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355113} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ca1022-57ef-510a-a692-20c04cb6a494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356090} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b69677-a3c4-5a4a-8fd8-58a0444592ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356380} {:answer/id #uuid "fe84379a-3267-576b-9bab-8baa1faa5368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4b69677-a3c4-5a4a-8fd8-58a0444592ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356380} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab27b24-a4f1-5208-81ee-7394385c2c05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e96ec148-dcd3-5736-b705-6d0e6370e151" :question/math-academy-id "q-93968" :question/problem "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =18-8-7 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b58f4ff-b6ed-5df6-b04f-137e285d5460" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Linear Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cde0db6-0613-5460-949f-eec249faca4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423312} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf3348c-7007-546d-af8d-511a3c29d678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423321} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb3e496-52aa-5e82-a11b-96ca9606f2b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423325} {:answer/id #uuid "6fefea64-9455-5b69-8388-8876d583feb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423326} {:answer/id #uuid "a616642f-842c-5